			"path": "examples/window/Window.cpp-simstep-72dfabb8-9fa7-4a1a-9c8b-bce364ea80c6",
			"fileName": "Window.cpp",
			"wiki": "The application's `main` function initializes and creates a window object. This example uses `sf::Window`, but `sf::RenderWindow` is also common. It specifies the window's dimensions, title, style, and context settings.",
			"cellName": "Application Creates Window - Window.cpp:L32-34",
			"cellId": "eaa6c395-9c69-47a7-81f2-3c3c3fa1a306",
			"visible": true,
			"startLine": 32,
			"endLine": 34,
			"parentCellId": "409cb91b-9bdd-45e6-8789-06ec635fa04a",
			"parentPath": "examples/window/Window.cpp"
		},
		"25ac6a69-0f14-4708-b107-0c112ea57204": {
			"path": "25ac6a69-0f14-4708-b107-0c112ea57204",
			"cellName": "Window Constructor Invokes `create` - Window.hpp:L165",
			"cellId": "25ac6a69-0f14-4708-b107-0c112ea57204",
			"visible": true,
			"parentCellId": "bfe9ab1f-f292-4bf0-a28d-167009fa6e73"
		},
		"include/SFML/Window/Window.hpp-simstep-4178e2dd-ca7f-4258-a28a-0678d6f89c27": {
			"path": "include/SFML/Window/Window.hpp-simstep-4178e2dd-ca7f-4258-a28a-0678d6f89c27",
			"fileName": "Window.hpp",
			"wiki": "The `sf::Window` constructor delegates the actual creation logic to its virtual `create` method. This method, in turn, calls the platform-agnostic `sf::WindowBase` to handle the creation of the underlying OS-specific window implementation.",
			"cellName": "Window Constructor Invokes `create` - Window.hpp:L165",
			"cellId": "25ac6a69-0f14-4708-b107-0c112ea57204",
			"visible": true,
			"startLine": 165,
			"endLine": 165,
			"parentCellId": "bfe9ab1f-f292-4bf0-a28d-167009fa6e73",
			"parentPath": "include/SFML/Window/Window.hpp"
		},
		"55956850-c89c-44e9-a723-4c5eb5bc9e78": {
			"path": "55956850-c89c-44e9-a723-4c5eb5bc9e78",
			"cellName": "Native OS Window Creation - WindowImpl.hpp:L157",
			"cellId": "55956850-c89c-44e9-a723-4c5eb5bc9e78",
			"visible": true,
			"parentCellId": "0d337467-43b2-41a8-8563-773892a40b14"
		},
		"src/SFML/Window/WindowImpl.hpp-simstep-e0154805-096e-4b0a-8e83-022e2e9d20da": {
			"path": "src/SFML/Window/WindowImpl.hpp-simstep-e0154805-096e-4b0a-8e83-022e2e9d20da",
			"fileName": "WindowImpl.hpp",
			"wiki": "The platform-specific `WindowImpl` class uses native OS APIs (e.g., Win32 API, X11, Cocoa) to create the actual window and its associated graphics context. Once created, it holds a native handle to this window.",
			"cellName": "Native OS Window Creation - WindowImpl.hpp:L157",
			"cellId": "55956850-c89c-44e9-a723-4c5eb5bc9e78",
			"visible": true,
			"startLine": 157,
			"endLine": 157,
			"parentCellId": "0d337467-43b2-41a8-8563-773892a40b14",
			"parentPath": "src/SFML/Window/WindowImpl.hpp"
		},
		"b40e18a5-1478-41fc-91ce-d4b416872b7d": {
			"path": "b40e18a5-1478-41fc-91ce-d4b416872b7d",
			"cellName": "Enter Main Application Loop - Window.cpp:L142",
			"cellId": "b40e18a5-1478-41fc-91ce-d4b416872b7d",
			"visible": true,
			"parentCellId": "409cb91b-9bdd-45e6-8789-06ec635fa04a"
		},
		"examples/window/Window.cpp-simstep-eada8035-fca7-4aa1-9525-f98f9a658618": {
			"path": "examples/window/Window.cpp-simstep-eada8035-fca7-4aa1-9525-f98f9a658618",
			"fileName": "Window.cpp",
			"wiki": "With the window successfully created, the application enters its main loop. The loop's continuation is controlled by the `window.isOpen()` method.",
			"cellName": "Enter Main Application Loop - Window.cpp:L142",
			"cellId": "b40e18a5-1478-41fc-91ce-d4b416872b7d",
			"visible": true,
			"startLine": 142,
			"endLine": 142,
			"parentCellId": "409cb91b-9bdd-45e6-8789-06ec635fa04a",
			"parentPath": "examples/window/Window.cpp"
		},
		"54326259-f66c-42d4-8703-b21c0fab1d3e": {
			"path": "54326259-f66c-42d4-8703-b21c0fab1d3e",
			"cellName": "Poll for Window Events - Window.cpp:L145",
			"cellId": "54326259-f66c-42d4-8703-b21c0fab1d3e",
			"visible": true,
			"parentCellId": "409cb91b-9bdd-45e6-8789-06ec635fa04a"
		},
		"examples/window/Window.cpp-simstep-4dc20f3e-e6c5-427d-8cf5-ec6de723cac6": {
			"path": "examples/window/Window.cpp-simstep-4dc20f3e-e6c5-427d-8cf5-ec6de723cac6",
			"fileName": "Window.cpp",
			"wiki": "Inside the main loop, the application calls `window.pollEvent()` to retrieve events from the window's event queue, such as user input or window state changes.",
			"cellName": "Poll for Window Events - Window.cpp:L145",
			"cellId": "54326259-f66c-42d4-8703-b21c0fab1d3e",
			"visible": true,
			"startLine": 145,
			"endLine": 145,
			"parentCellId": "409cb91b-9bdd-45e6-8789-06ec635fa04a",
			"parentPath": "examples/window/Window.cpp"
		},
		"c1848dd0-ddee-4eff-8c75-62b4e11a18cc": {
			"path": "c1848dd0-ddee-4eff-8c75-62b4e11a18cc",
			"cellName": "OS Event Processing - WindowImpl.cpp:L254",
			"cellId": "c1848dd0-ddee-4eff-8c75-62b4e11a18cc",
			"visible": true,
			"parentCellId": "68858b34-c441-4f4a-afb8-53178f20ad3f"
		},
		"src/SFML/Window/WindowImpl.cpp-simstep-fb87c0fa-9648-4b9f-b633-115a36ae36c6": {
			"path": "src/SFML/Window/WindowImpl.cpp-simstep-fb87c0fa-9648-4b9f-b633-115a36ae36c6",
			"fileName": "WindowImpl.cpp",
			"wiki": "The `WindowImpl`'s `pollEvent` method calls `populateEventQueue`. This function queries the operating system for pending messages, translates them from their native format into `sf::Event` objects, and pushes them onto an internal event queue.",
			"cellName": "OS Event Processing - WindowImpl.cpp:L254",
			"cellId": "c1848dd0-ddee-4eff-8c75-62b4e11a18cc",
			"visible": true,
			"startLine": 254,
			"endLine": 254,
			"parentCellId": "68858b34-c441-4f4a-afb8-53178f20ad3f",
			"parentPath": "src/SFML/Window/WindowImpl.cpp"
		},
		"123cd87b-b4fa-4f50-91e5-df6edb3642d0": {
			"path": "123cd87b-b4fa-4f50-91e5-df6edb3642d0",
			"cellName": "Application Handles `Closed` Event - Window.cpp:L148-151",
			"cellId": "123cd87b-b4fa-4f50-91e5-df6edb3642d0",
			"visible": true,
			"parentCellId": "409cb91b-9bdd-45e6-8789-06ec635fa04a"
		},
		"examples/window/Window.cpp-simstep-7f62ffee-a4ae-4578-bf0d-1dfed26906fd": {
			"path": "examples/window/Window.cpp-simstep-7f62ffee-a4ae-4578-bf0d-1dfed26906fd",
			"fileName": "Window.cpp",
			"wiki": "The application code inspects the event. Upon receiving an `sf::Event::Closed` event (typically triggered by the user clicking the window's close button), it calls `window.close()` to initiate the window shutdown process.",
			"cellName": "Application Handles `Closed` Event - Window.cpp:L148-151",
			"cellId": "123cd87b-b4fa-4f50-91e5-df6edb3642d0",
			"visible": true,
			"startLine": 148,
			"endLine": 151,
			"parentCellId": "409cb91b-9bdd-45e6-8789-06ec635fa04a",
			"parentPath": "examples/window/Window.cpp"
		},
		"37117a88-45ef-4586-b07a-5707a216b6d2": {
			"path": "37117a88-45ef-4586-b07a-5707a216b6d2",
			"cellName": "Window Implementation Destroyed - WindowBase.cpp:L128-129",
			"cellId": "37117a88-45ef-4586-b07a-5707a216b6d2",
			"visible": true,
			"parentCellId": "a941e50d-ce2a-4cc7-98dc-135e581080f3"
		},
		"src/SFML/Window/WindowBase.cpp-simstep-5fca8efd-ec9f-442c-8e42-5061bfde1335": {
			"path": "src/SFML/Window/WindowBase.cpp-simstep-5fca8efd-ec9f-442c-8e42-5061bfde1335",
			"fileName": "WindowBase.cpp",
			"wiki": "The `sf::WindowBase::close()` method resets the `std::unique_ptr` holding the platform-specific implementation (`m_impl`). This triggers the destructor of the `WindowImpl` subclass, which calls the necessary OS APIs to destroy the native window.",
			"cellName": "Window Implementation Destroyed - WindowBase.cpp:L128-129",
			"cellId": "37117a88-45ef-4586-b07a-5707a216b6d2",
			"visible": true,
			"startLine": 128,
			"endLine": 129,
			"parentCellId": "a941e50d-ce2a-4cc7-98dc-135e581080f3",
			"parentPath": "src/SFML/Window/WindowBase.cpp"
		},
		"b6e5c505-8299-4c02-a548-2061d6e389be": {
			"path": "b6e5c505-8299-4c02-a548-2061d6e389be",
			"cellName": "Application Termination - Window.cpp:L185",
			"cellId": "b6e5c505-8299-4c02-a548-2061d6e389be",
			"visible": true,
			"parentCellId": "409cb91b-9bdd-45e6-8789-06ec635fa04a"
		},
		"examples/window/Window.cpp-simstep-cbf54c1d-1d98-4699-aab2-4e9b14c4e30a": {
			"path": "examples/window/Window.cpp-simstep-cbf54c1d-1d98-4699-aab2-4e9b14c4e30a",
			"fileName": "Window.cpp",
			"wiki": "After the main loop exits, the `sf::Window` object's destructor is called as it goes out of scope. The `main` function then returns, and the application terminates.",
			"cellName": "Application Termination - Window.cpp:L185",
			"cellId": "b6e5c505-8299-4c02-a548-2061d6e389be",
			"visible": true,
			"startLine": 185,
			"endLine": 185,
			"parentCellId": "409cb91b-9bdd-45e6-8789-06ec635fa04a",
			"parentPath": "examples/window/Window.cpp"
		},
		"1d22e6c2-6218-4cd7-849f-7e1268bed1e3": {
			"path": "1d22e6c2-6218-4cd7-849f-7e1268bed1e3",
