		"c48172ff-f50d-49fc-94c9-35c9bfea68ef": {
			"path": "c48172ff-f50d-49fc-94c9-35c9bfea68ef",
			"cellName": "Load Shader From File - Shader.cpp:L283-285",
			"cellId": "c48172ff-f50d-49fc-94c9-35c9bfea68ef",
			"visible": true,
			"parentCellId": "7b810f43-1fd2-4266-8010-c366e141b6a1"
		},
		"examples/shader/Shader.cpp-simstep-62834f02-8cf2-4c30-a082-c0c36f3b0165": {
			"path": "examples/shader/Shader.cpp-simstep-62834f02-8cf2-4c30-a082-c0c36f3b0165",
			"fileName": "Shader.cpp",
			"wiki": "The application starts by checking if shaders are available. Then, it attempts to load a custom GLSL fragment shader from a file ('pixelate.frag') into an `sf::Shader` object. This function reads the shader source code, compiles it, and links it into a shader program managed by the `sf::Shader` instance.",
			"cellName": "Load Shader From File - Shader.cpp:L283-285",
			"cellId": "c48172ff-f50d-49fc-94c9-35c9bfea68ef",
			"visible": true,
			"startLine": 283,
			"endLine": 285,
			"parentCellId": "7b810f43-1fd2-4266-8010-c366e141b6a1",
			"parentPath": "examples/shader/Shader.cpp"
		},
		"c1485b8e-90fa-490a-bdaf-6d82816b6545": {
			"path": "c1485b8e-90fa-490a-bdaf-6d82816b6545",
			"cellName": "Configure Initial Shader Uniform - Shader.cpp:L41",
			"cellId": "c1485b8e-90fa-490a-bdaf-6d82816b6545",
			"visible": true,
			"parentCellId": "7b810f43-1fd2-4266-8010-c366e141b6a1"
		},
		"examples/shader/Shader.cpp-simstep-ac954dfc-f8ed-4ef1-ba45-0294f47650dc": {
			"path": "examples/shader/Shader.cpp-simstep-ac954dfc-f8ed-4ef1-ba45-0294f47650dc",
			"fileName": "Shader.cpp",
			"wiki": "Inside the `Pixelate` effect's constructor, an initial uniform variable named 'texture' is set. It is assigned the special value `sf::Shader::CurrentTexture`, which instructs the shader to use the texture of the object being drawn at render time.",
			"cellName": "Configure Initial Shader Uniform - Shader.cpp:L41",
			"cellId": "c1485b8e-90fa-490a-bdaf-6d82816b6545",
			"visible": true,
			"startLine": 41,
			"endLine": 41,
			"parentCellId": "7b810f43-1fd2-4266-8010-c366e141b6a1",
			"parentPath": "examples/shader/Shader.cpp"
		},
		"3a731d50-712d-4ea0-aed0-0db48cc5f34a": {
			"path": "3a731d50-712d-4ea0-aed0-0db48cc5f34a",
			"cellName": "Update Dynamic Uniform in Game Loop - Shader.cpp:L46-47",
			"cellId": "3a731d50-712d-4ea0-aed0-0db48cc5f34a",
			"visible": true,
			"parentCellId": "7b810f43-1fd2-4266-8010-c366e141b6a1"
		},
		"examples/shader/Shader.cpp-simstep-d20cecc3-986d-4ec2-94fd-98e57b580531": {
			"path": "examples/shader/Shader.cpp-simstep-d20cecc3-986d-4ec2-94fd-98e57b580531",
			"fileName": "Shader.cpp",
			"wiki": "In each frame of the main loop, the `update` method of the current effect is called. For the `Pixelate` effect, this dynamically calculates a `pixel_threshold` value based on the mouse's X and Y coordinates and sends it to the shader via `setUniform`. This allows the visual effect to be interactive.",
			"cellName": "Update Dynamic Uniform in Game Loop - Shader.cpp:L46-47",
			"cellId": "3a731d50-712d-4ea0-aed0-0db48cc5f34a",
			"visible": true,
			"startLine": 46,
			"endLine": 47,
			"parentCellId": "7b810f43-1fd2-4266-8010-c366e141b6a1",
			"parentPath": "examples/shader/Shader.cpp"
		},
		"4733a521-4569-4cb6-9dbd-69f324158e9c": {
			"path": "4733a521-4569-4cb6-9dbd-69f324158e9c",
			"cellName": "Prepare Render States for Drawing - Shader.cpp:L51",
			"cellId": "4733a521-4569-4cb6-9dbd-69f324158e9c",
			"visible": true,
			"parentCellId": "7b810f43-1fd2-4266-8010-c366e141b6a1"
		},
		"examples/shader/Shader.cpp-simstep-41a0c2c6-b4b4-454e-ac89-3a458c6ab9a9": {
			"path": "examples/shader/Shader.cpp-simstep-41a0c2c6-b4b4-454e-ac89-3a458c6ab9a9",
			"fileName": "Shader.cpp",
			"wiki": "When it's time to draw the effect, the `draw` method is called. It configures an `sf::RenderStates` object by assigning its `shader` member a pointer to the `Pixelate` effect's `sf::Shader` instance. This object bundles all the necessary states for rendering.",
			"cellName": "Prepare Render States for Drawing - Shader.cpp:L51",
			"cellId": "4733a521-4569-4cb6-9dbd-69f324158e9c",
			"visible": true,
			"startLine": 51,
			"endLine": 51,
			"parentCellId": "7b810f43-1fd2-4266-8010-c366e141b6a1",
			"parentPath": "examples/shader/Shader.cpp"
		},
		"5be5dbf4-e09e-4e40-ad9d-c9f82a7421d2": {
			"path": "5be5dbf4-e09e-4e40-ad9d-c9f82a7421d2",
			"cellName": "Render Target Applies Shader - Sprite.cpp:L117-124",
			"cellId": "5be5dbf4-e09e-4e40-ad9d-c9f82a7421d2",
			"visible": true,
			"parentCellId": "eafb8954-bf60-455b-8504-16dd41031d48"
		},
		"src/SFML/Graphics/Sprite.cpp-simstep-60c95fda-2d0f-4852-85f8-f077f4291b32": {
			"path": "src/SFML/Graphics/Sprite.cpp-simstep-60c95fda-2d0f-4852-85f8-f077f4291b32",
			"fileName": "Sprite.cpp",
			"wiki": "The `RenderTarget` receives the drawable and the render states. The sprite's `draw` method is called, which combines the sprite's own transform with the render states, sets the texture, and calls the low-level draw function. This function is responsible for binding the specified shader and texture before issuing the actual draw command to the GPU.",
			"cellName": "Render Target Applies Shader - Sprite.cpp:L117-124",
			"cellId": "5be5dbf4-e09e-4e40-ad9d-c9f82a7421d2",
			"visible": true,
			"startLine": 117,
			"endLine": 124,
			"parentCellId": "eafb8954-bf60-455b-8504-16dd41031d48",
			"parentPath": "src/SFML/Graphics/Sprite.cpp"
		},
		"f997bd47-7dc3-4346-b71e-90897b7d7c7f": {
			"path": "f997bd47-7dc3-4346-b71e-90897b7d7c7f",
			"cellName": "GPU Executes Fragment Shader - pixelate.frag:L1-15",
			"cellId": "f997bd47-7dc3-4346-b71e-90897b7d7c7f",
			"visible": true,
			"parentCellId": "8234d4c4-4301-49fa-9629-104d01ee1972"
		},
		"examples/shader/resources/pixelate.frag-simstep-c8eb3f05-fc35-4fe0-971d-38c484e83cfa": {
			"path": "examples/shader/resources/pixelate.frag-simstep-c8eb3f05-fc35-4fe0-971d-38c484e83cfa",
			"fileName": "pixelate.frag",
			"wiki": "The GPU's graphics pipeline executes the fragment shader for each pixel of the sprite. The shader code reads the `pixel_threshold` uniform, calculates a new texture coordinate by rounding the original one, samples the color from this new coordinate in the 'texture' uniform, and outputs the final pixel color to the screen, creating the pixelated effect.",
			"cellName": "GPU Executes Fragment Shader - pixelate.frag:L1-15",
			"cellId": "f997bd47-7dc3-4346-b71e-90897b7d7c7f",
			"visible": true,
			"startLine": 1,
			"endLine": 15,
			"parentCellId": "8234d4c4-4301-49fa-9629-104d01ee1972",
			"parentPath": "examples/shader/resources/pixelate.frag"
		},
		"cf01911c-3c8b-4d74-93a1-08f4b6660091": {
