		},
		"6584d727-f333-45ba-bf0a-2d9195ae894b": {
			"path": "6584d727-f333-45ba-bf0a-2d9195ae894b",
			"cellName": "View.hpp",
			"cellId": "6584d727-f333-45ba-bf0a-2d9195ae894b",
			"visible": true,
			"parentCellId": "5cd1a142-9555-4c25-b56f-b766738ee3de"
		},
		"6ad4b3df-4215-47b7-9339-1d6c1f68a1e5": {
			"path": "6ad4b3df-4215-47b7-9339-1d6c1f68a1e5",
			"cellName": "Flow 1: Event Handling - Window Resize Event - Tennis.cpp:L152-158",
			"cellId": "6ad4b3df-4215-47b7-9339-1d6c1f68a1e5",
			"visible": true,
			"parentCellId": "375d9713-4499-4c06-8630-3364d95ebb0e"
		},
		"examples/tennis/Tennis.cpp-simstep-fec1e926-9641-4251-974f-62f2eab1a155": {
			"path": "examples/tennis/Tennis.cpp-simstep-fec1e926-9641-4251-974f-62f2eab1a155",
			"fileName": "Tennis.cpp",
			"wiki": "The application's main loop polls for events. When a window resize event occurs, the application logic creates a new `sf::View` to adjust the game's viewport to the new window dimensions, ensuring the content scales correctly.",
			"cellName": "Flow 1: Event Handling - Window Resize Event - Tennis.cpp:L152-158",
			"cellId": "6ad4b3df-4215-47b7-9339-1d6c1f68a1e5",
			"visible": true,
			"startLine": 152,
			"endLine": 158,
			"parentCellId": "375d9713-4499-4c06-8630-3364d95ebb0e",
			"parentPath": "examples/tennis/Tennis.cpp"
		},
		"254d835e-a216-49ae-b94e-ef27399bf403": {
			"path": "254d835e-a216-49ae-b94e-ef27399bf403",
			"cellName": "Flow 1: API Call - Update RenderTarget's View - RenderTarget.cpp:L255-259",
			"cellId": "254d835e-a216-49ae-b94e-ef27399bf403",
			"visible": true,
			"parentCellId": "628af0bb-2c3b-46d5-af54-22e9d6f3d454"
		},
		"src/SFML/Graphics/RenderTarget.cpp-simstep-9f41a771-a341-4f62-89ac-4ff1b91e5066": {
			"path": "src/SFML/Graphics/RenderTarget.cpp-simstep-9f41a771-a341-4f62-89ac-4ff1b91e5066",
			"fileName": "RenderTarget.cpp",
			"wiki": "The `sf::RenderTarget::setView` method is invoked. It updates the render target's internal `sf::View` instance with the new view and sets a flag (`m_cache.viewChanged`) to true, indicating that the rendering projection needs to be recalculated before the next draw call.",
			"cellName": "Flow 1: API Call - Update RenderTarget's View - RenderTarget.cpp:L255-259",
			"cellId": "254d835e-a216-49ae-b94e-ef27399bf403",
			"visible": true,
			"startLine": 255,
			"endLine": 259,
			"parentCellId": "628af0bb-2c3b-46d5-af54-22e9d6f3d454",
			"parentPath": "src/SFML/Graphics/RenderTarget.cpp"
		},
		"cb81c998-e644-44b0-be45-12e389a56845": {
			"path": "cb81c998-e644-44b0-be45-12e389a56845",
			"cellName": "Flow 2: API Call - Set View Center (Panning) - View.cpp:L48-53",
			"cellId": "cb81c998-e644-44b0-be45-12e389a56845",
			"visible": true,
			"parentCellId": "88819e54-d79c-48de-9f08-a46aa3bf20c2"
		},
		"src/SFML/Graphics/View.cpp-simstep-b9fffd01-207b-4116-a63d-33b1315600f6": {
			"path": "src/SFML/Graphics/View.cpp-simstep-b9fffd01-207b-4116-a63d-33b1315600f6",
			"fileName": "View.cpp",
			"wiki": "The application calls `sf::View::setCenter` with the character's new position. This method updates the view's internal center coordinates and invalidates the cached transformation matrices by setting `m_transformUpdated` and `m_invTransformUpdated` to `false`.",
			"cellName": "Flow 2: API Call - Set View Center (Panning) - View.cpp:L48-53",
			"cellId": "cb81c998-e644-44b0-be45-12e389a56845",
			"visible": true,
			"startLine": 48,
			"endLine": 53,
			"parentCellId": "88819e54-d79c-48de-9f08-a46aa3bf20c2",
			"parentPath": "src/SFML/Graphics/View.cpp"
		},
		"eecc515e-1d43-4c53-9281-d1405689d826": {
			"path": "eecc515e-1d43-4c53-9281-d1405689d826",
			"cellName": "Flow 2: API Call - Update RenderTarget with Panned View - RenderTarget.cpp:L255-259",
			"cellId": "eecc515e-1d43-4c53-9281-d1405689d826",
			"visible": true,
			"parentCellId": "628af0bb-2c3b-46d5-af54-22e9d6f3d454"
		},
		"src/SFML/Graphics/RenderTarget.cpp-simstep-053fa3fa-5441-47e3-a3a8-691cd385d118": {
			"path": "src/SFML/Graphics/RenderTarget.cpp-simstep-053fa3fa-5441-47e3-a3a8-691cd385d118",
			"fileName": "RenderTarget.cpp",
			"wiki": "The `sf::RenderTarget::setView` method is called again, copying the panned view into its internal state and flagging that the view has changed, ensuring the new camera position is used for rendering.",
			"cellName": "Flow 2: API Call - Update RenderTarget with Panned View - RenderTarget.cpp:L255-259",
			"cellId": "eecc515e-1d43-4c53-9281-d1405689d826",
			"visible": true,
			"startLine": 255,
			"endLine": 259,
			"parentCellId": "628af0bb-2c3b-46d5-af54-22e9d6f3d454",
			"parentPath": "src/SFML/Graphics/RenderTarget.cpp"
		},
		"612c7a69-65d6-48d8-8238-0127aa9d9fdd": {
			"path": "612c7a69-65d6-48d8-8238-0127aa9d9fdd",
			"cellName": "Flow 3: API Call - Zoom View - View.cpp:L147-150",
			"cellId": "612c7a69-65d6-48d8-8238-0127aa9d9fdd",
			"visible": true,
			"parentCellId": "88819e54-d79c-48de-9f08-a46aa3bf20c2"
		},
		"src/SFML/Graphics/View.cpp-simstep-9d1fc73f-ac3e-4acc-b1a7-175b5f7bd20a": {
			"path": "src/SFML/Graphics/View.cpp-simstep-9d1fc73f-ac3e-4acc-b1a7-175b5f7bd20a",
			"fileName": "View.cpp",
			"wiki": "The application calls the `sf::View::zoom` method with the specified factor. This is a convenience function that multiplies the current view's size by the factor and calls `setSize` internally.",
			"cellName": "Flow 3: API Call - Zoom View - View.cpp:L147-150",
			"cellId": "612c7a69-65d6-48d8-8238-0127aa9d9fdd",
			"visible": true,
			"startLine": 147,
			"endLine": 150,
			"parentCellId": "88819e54-d79c-48de-9f08-a46aa3bf20c2",
			"parentPath": "src/SFML/Graphics/View.cpp"
		},
		"94a3e70d-5466-4ef0-9fed-fe254dfc17a9": {
			"path": "94a3e70d-5466-4ef0-9fed-fe254dfc17a9",
			"cellName": "Flow 3: API Call - Update RenderTarget with Zoomed View - RenderTarget.cpp:L255-259",
			"cellId": "94a3e70d-5466-4ef0-9fed-fe254dfc17a9",
			"visible": true,
			"parentCellId": "628af0bb-2c3b-46d5-af54-22e9d6f3d454"
		},
		"src/SFML/Graphics/RenderTarget.cpp-simstep-a0766046-3fc4-450d-9391-de86a22a23be": {
			"path": "src/SFML/Graphics/RenderTarget.cpp-simstep-a0766046-3fc4-450d-9391-de86a22a23be",
			"fileName": "RenderTarget.cpp",
			"wiki": "Finally, `sf::RenderTarget::setView` is called with the zoomed view. The render target updates its internal view and flags it as changed, so the new zoom level will be reflected in subsequent draw calls.",
			"cellName": "Flow 3: API Call - Update RenderTarget with Zoomed View - RenderTarget.cpp:L255-259",
			"cellId": "94a3e70d-5466-4ef0-9fed-fe254dfc17a9",
			"visible": true,
			"startLine": 255,
			"endLine": 259,
			"parentCellId": "628af0bb-2c3b-46d5-af54-22e9d6f3d454",
			"parentPath": "src/SFML/Graphics/RenderTarget.cpp"
		},
		"deca5615-7641-4b95-939c-ccb1fd8ddc5f": {
