		"Handle real-time user input and window events": {
			"name": "Handle real-time user input and window events",
			"simSteps": [
				{
					"simStepId": "ce2c4e08-6020-4b3d-8882-6269f392d994",
					"diagramNodeId": "0a3b7921-613e-440e-867d-9a51d8b814c0",
					"simStepLabel": "Event Polling: Application Polls for Events",
					"simStepDescription": "The application's main loop continuously calls `window.pollEvent()` to check for and retrieve pending events from the operating system, such as keyboard presses, mouse movements, or window close requests.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "examples/window/Window.cpp",
						"startLine": "144",
						"endLine": "145",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"window",
							"event",
							"pollEvent"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"window.isOpen()\": true}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"event\": {\"type\": \"KeyPressed\", \"key\": {\"code\": \"Escape\", \"scancode\": \"Escape\", \"alt\": false, \"control\": false, \"shift\": false, \"system\": false}}}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "d0e9b187-a9c7-4461-b166-2a320815837e",
					"diagramNodeId": "557c14af-b484-4c54-ba43-cc411bb3f780",
					"simStepLabel": "Event Polling: Event Poll Request",
					"simStepDescription": "The call to `pollEvent()` is propagated from the application code to the `sf::WindowBase` class, initiating the process of checking the internal event queue.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "include/SFML/Window/WindowBase.hpp",
						"startLine": "228",
						"endLine": "228",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"pollEvent"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{}",
					"outputDataExample": "{}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "a2f2577d-ba8f-433f-953c-1842edaa0f85",
					"diagramNodeId": "e06e5bf3-5d3b-44be-95a6-3af785a81834",
					"simStepLabel": "Event Polling: WindowBase Forwards Poll Request",
					"simStepDescription": "The `sf::WindowBase::pollEvent()` method delegates the call to its platform-specific implementation (`m_impl`), which handles the direct interaction with the OS windowing system.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/SFML/Window/WindowBase.cpp",
						"startLine": "138",
						"endLine": "147",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"m_impl",
							"pollEvent",
							"filterEvent"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"m_impl->pollEvent() call\": \"initiated\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "84aa7fc8-5408-451c-9ac8-175b0bb550bd",
					"diagramNodeId": "ba2301c7-a1e1-4748-b29c-b37353cd155c",
					"simStepLabel": "Event Polling: Request to Platform-Specific Implementation",
					"simStepDescription": "The call is passed to the `pollEvent` method of the concrete `WindowImpl` class, which is responsible for managing the event queue.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/SFML/Window/WindowImpl.hpp",
						"startLine": "148",
						"endLine": "148",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"pollEvent"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{}",
					"outputDataExample": "{}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "85bb3f1b-e4c7-48f2-8f6d-5d744f034fc7",
					"diagramNodeId": "3d9264a5-efa5-491e-a0bb-240d9f4d0a7b",
					"simStepLabel": "Event Polling: WindowImpl Populates and Polls Event Queue",
					"simStepDescription": "The `WindowImpl::pollEvent()` method first checks if its internal event queue is empty. If so, it calls `populateEventQueue()` to fetch new events from the operating system. It then returns the next event from the front of the queue.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/SFML/Window/WindowImpl.cpp",
						"startLine": "250",
						"endLine": "260",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"m_events",
							"populateEventQueue",
							"popEvent"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"m_events.empty()\": true}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"event\": {\"type\": \"MouseButtonPressed\", \"mouseButton\": {\"button\": \"Left\", \"position\": {\"x\": 512, \"y\": 384}}}}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "6d20b694-c48d-4765-ba3f-b7b2c2a4a1f6",
					"diagramNodeId": "ed06d0e1-7e0b-43c3-88cb-77ea23d02de4",
					"simStepLabel": "Event Polling: OS Event Data Transmission",
					"simStepDescription": "The platform-specific implementation reads raw event data from the operating system. This raw data is then translated into a standardized `sf::Event` format.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/SFML/Window/DRM/InputImpl.cpp",
						"startLine": "371",
						"endLine": "372",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"fd",
							"inputEvent",
							"bytesRead"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"raw_event\": {\"type\": \"EV_KEY\", \"code\": 272, \"value\": 1}}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"raw_event\": {\"type\": \"EV_KEY\", \"code\": 272, \"value\": 1}}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "1754f7ca-d3c3-42e5-977b-fbb1e2438985",
					"diagramNodeId": "33429860-81eb-45c6-ae04-b56c67b15f8f",
					"simStepLabel": "Event Polling: Platform Translates OS Event to SFML Event",
					"simStepDescription": "The platform-specific implementation code interprets the raw OS event data (e.g., a key code, mouse coordinates) and constructs the corresponding `sf::Event` subtype, such as `sf::Event::KeyPressed` or `sf::Event::MouseMoved`.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/SFML/Window/DRM/InputImpl.cpp",
						"startLine": "376",
						"endLine": "382",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"toMouseButton",
							"mouseMap",
							"mousePos",
							"sf::Event::MouseButtonPressed"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"inputEvent\": {\"type\": \"EV_KEY\", \"code\": 272, \"value\": 1}}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"event\": {\"type\": \"MouseButtonPressed\", \"mouseButton\": {\"button\": \"Left\", \"position\": {\"x\": 512, \"y\": 384}}}}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "e7f54041-6183-421a-8bfa-1963e743b083",
					"diagramNodeId": "7d82aff3-ba55-4cd3-886b-918a7a695e11",
					"simStepLabel": "Event Polling: Push Event to Queue",
					"simStepDescription": "The newly created `sf::Event` is pushed into the internal event queue, waiting to be retrieved by the application.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/SFML/Window/DRM/InputImpl.cpp",
						"startLine": "306",
						"endLine": "312",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"pushEvent",
							"eventQueue",
							"maxQueue"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"event\": {\"type\": \"MouseButtonPressed\", \"mouseButton\": {\"button\": \"Left\", \"position\": {\"x\": 512, \"y\": 384}}}}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"event\": {\"type\": \"MouseButtonPressed\", \"mouseButton\": {\"button\": \"Left\", \"position\": {\"x\": 512, \"y\": 384}}}}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "b2461801-db87-4f53-ad24-96e735a7f67b",
					"diagramNodeId": "2933c66a-fad6-4cef-a5ba-d2a8d0c0aaf4",
					"simStepLabel": "Event Polling: Application Handles Specific Event",
					"simStepDescription": "The application receives the polled event. It then uses type-safe methods like `event->is<T>()` or `event->getIf<T>()` to identify the event type and access its specific data, executing the appropriate logic.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "examples/event_handling/EventHandling.cpp",
						"startLine": "131",
						"endLine": "134",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"event",
							"is",
							"m_log"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"event\": {\"type\": \"MouseButtonPressed\", \"mouseButton\": {\"button\": \"Left\", \"position\": {\"x\": 512, \"y\": 384}}}}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"logMessage\": \"Mouse Pressed\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "6a57528f-f4b7-4c34-89fb-a9ee236ffdc9",
					"diagramNodeId": "596e1f26-08c2-4d47-917a-8e98749348aa",
					"simStepLabel": "Real-Time Query: Application Checks Key Press",
					"simStepDescription": "For continuous input like character movement, the application directly queries the real-time state of a specific key by calling `sf::Keyboard::isKeyPressed()`. This check is typically performed every frame.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "examples/tennis/Tennis.cpp",
						"startLine": "163",
						"endLine": "163",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"sf::Keyboard::isKeyPressed",
							"sf::Keyboard::Key::Up"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"key\": \"Up\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"isPressed\": true}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "f4aa3b0b-177c-46a5-b1e8-ee16b0a67bb5",
					"diagramNodeId": "3619b4db-df9e-42c9-9b2a-625cd28e9462",
					"simStepLabel": "Real-Time Query: Key State Query",
					"simStepDescription": "The request to check the key's state is passed down to the SFML backend.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "include/SFML/Window/Keyboard.hpp",
						"startLine": "347",
						"endLine": "347",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"isKeyPressed"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"key\": \"Up\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"key\": \"Up\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "2a4a152c-3d4e-4d78-a767-64190e681d3c",
					"diagramNodeId": "c9128104-9970-4676-99e4-2457ec9db1d7",
					"simStepLabel": "Real-Time Query: sf::Keyboard Forwards Call",
					"simStepDescription": "The static `sf::Keyboard::isKeyPressed` function acts as a public API entry point and forwards the call to the internal, platform-agnostic `InputImpl` module.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/SFML/Window/Keyboard.cpp",
						"startLine": "36",
						"endLine": "39",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"priv::InputImpl::isKeyPressed",
							"key"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"key\": \"Up\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"key\": \"Up\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "6604c3f3-2a1e-4a1d-9f9c-e75144cfe178",
					"diagramNodeId": "47c809a5-2990-4c88-bc2c-97ab45ee238f",
					"simStepLabel": "Real-Time Query: Request to Platform-Specific Implementation",
					"simStepDescription": "The call is routed from the generic `InputImpl` to the specific implementation for the target operating system (e.g., Windows, macOS, Linux).",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/SFML/Window/InputImpl.hpp",
						"startLine": "45",
						"endLine": "45",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"isKeyPressed"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"key\": \"Up\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"key\": \"Up\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "636043a1-0498-4913-b7e6-5863f7a0fc48",
					"diagramNodeId": "bc33b19f-302c-43e9-ae39-fc636dee075e",
					"simStepLabel": "Real-Time Query: OS Queries Key State",
					"simStepDescription": "The platform-specific code calls a native OS function (like `GetAsyncKeyState` on Windows) to get the instantaneous state of the physical key, bypassing the event queue.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/SFML/Window/Win32/InputImpl.cpp",
						"startLine": "589",
						"endLine": "593",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"isKeyPressed",
							"sfKeyToVirtualKey",
							"GetAsyncKeyState"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"key\": \"Up\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"virtualKey\": 38, \"isPressed\": true}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "6f7b3268-a6cd-445a-924b-585749bd8c96",
					"diagramNodeId": "55a6874e-0415-4d3d-9438-a4159b33f0b9",
					"simStepLabel": "Real-Time Query: Return Key State",
					"simStepDescription": "The boolean result (`true` for pressed, `false` for not pressed) is returned up the call stack.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/SFML/Window/Keyboard.cpp",
						"startLine": "36",
						"endLine": "39",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"isKeyPressed"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"isPressed\": true}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"isPressed\": true}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "bf2ed579-fb2b-4b49-9355-43b4f296595a",
					"diagramNodeId": "24e54584-9e26-498d-b7e2-6e570b28a2fa",
					"simStepLabel": "Real-Time Query: Application Uses Key State",
					"simStepDescription": "The application receives the boolean result and uses it to execute continuous game logic, such as moving a paddle.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "examples/tennis/Tennis.cpp",
						"startLine": "165",
						"endLine": "165",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"leftPaddle",
							"move",
							"paddleSpeed",
							"deltaTime"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"isPressed\": true, \"deltaTime\": 0.016}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"paddle.move.y\": -6.4}"
				}
			],
			"description": "<ul><li>SFML provides a simple yet powerful system for handling user interaction, which is essential for games and interactive applications</li><li>- Poll and process a queue of discrete events, such as a key being pressed (<code>sf::Event::KeyPressed</code>), the mouse being moved (<code>sf::Event::MouseMoved</code>), or the window being closed (<code>sf::Event::Closed</code>)</li><li>- Query the real-time state of the keyboard (<code>sf::Keyboard::isKeyPressed</code>) and mouse (<code>sf::Mouse::isButtonPressed</code>) directly, ideal for continuous actions like character movement</li><li>- Get input from other devices like joysticks and touchscreens</li></ul>",
			"simulationNodesAndEdges": {
