					"outputDataExample": "{\"surface\": {\"id\": \"render_texture_01\", \"size\": {\"width\": 800, \"height\": 600}, \"isSmooth\": true}}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "26a327de-bc00-459b-908a-c8fe7834a8b5",
					"diagramNodeId": "aa5ea8af-dd5a-4f12-ae83-fe97065392b4",
					"simStepLabel": "RenderTexture Ready for Drawing",
					"simStepDescription": "The newly created `sf::RenderTexture` is now available as a member of the 'Edge' effect object, ready to be used as a drawing target in the main application loop.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "examples/shader/Shader.cpp",
						"startLine": "486",
						"endLine": "486",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"currentEffect->update"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"surface\": {\"id\": \"render_texture_01\", \"size\": {\"width\": 800, \"height\": 600}, \"isSmooth\": true}}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"surface\": {\"id\": \"render_texture_01\", \"size\": {\"width\": 800, \"height\": 600}, \"isSmooth\": true}}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "61cad681-ad9e-4d87-a6e8-48970ebf4a44",
					"diagramNodeId": "76ab54d1-d312-4bb2-941d-adf1a51f152c",
					"simStepLabel": "Render Scene to Off-Screen Texture",
					"simStepDescription": "Within the `Edge::update` method, the `sf::RenderTexture` is first cleared. Then, various drawable objects, such as background and entity sprites, are drawn onto it. These drawing operations render into the texture's memory, not directly to the screen.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "examples/shader/Shader.cpp",
						"startLine": "174",
						"endLine": "192",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"m_surface",
							"m_surface.clear",
							"m_surface.draw",
							"backgroundSprite",
							"entity"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"time\": 1.25, \"mouse_position\": {\"x\": 0.5, \"y\": 0.5}}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"renderTextureState\": \"internal_buffer_contains_rendered_scene\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "b165b635-310c-4c8e-a568-4da32d2aeefb",
					"diagramNodeId": "da3eb302-67ad-4116-a873-7f8085fb44fe",
					"simStepLabel": "Transmit Drawable to RenderTarget",
					"simStepDescription": "The `RenderTarget::draw` method is invoked on the `sf::RenderTexture`, passing a drawable object (like `sf::Sprite`). This initiates the rendering pipeline for that object, directing its graphical output to the off-screen texture.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/SFML/Graphics/RenderTarget.cpp",
						"startLine": "338",
						"endLine": "341",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"draw",
							"drawable",
							"states"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"drawable_type\": \"sf::Sprite\", \"drawable_properties\": {\"texture\": \"entity.png\", \"position\": {\"x\": 350.0, \"y\": 250.0}}, \"render_states\": {\"blendMode\": \"BlendAlpha\", \"transform\": \"Identity\", \"shader\": null}}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"drawable_type\": \"sf::Sprite\", \"drawable_properties\": {\"texture\": \"entity.png\", \"position\": {\"x\": 350.0, \"y\": 250.0}}, \"render_states\": {\"blendMode\": \"BlendAlpha\", \"transform\": \"Identity\", \"shader\": null}}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "ca548921-31c6-450f-8b2f-78325a27232f",
					"diagramNodeId": "9b783e7a-3fc9-4d66-8653-94faa440c341",
					"simStepLabel": "Finalize Off-Screen Texture Content",
					"simStepDescription": "The `display()` method is called on the `sf::RenderTexture`. This finalizes the drawing operations performed on it, updating the internal texture with the rendered content and making it available for subsequent use.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "examples/shader/Shader.cpp",
						"startLine": "194",
						"endLine": "194",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"m_surface.display"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"renderTextureState\": \"internal_buffer_contains_rendered_scene\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"textureState\": \"updated_with_rendered_scene\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "52920bce-a04d-47ee-b097-dbd8d357bd64",
					"diagramNodeId": "c7bde6b5-2792-4d39-b0b7-c229c548bd29",
					"simStepLabel": "Off-Screen Texture Ready for Use",
					"simStepDescription": "The content of the `sf::RenderTexture` is now finalized and available as a standard `sf::Texture`. It is retrieved via `getTexture()` to be used in the next drawing stage.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "examples/shader/Shader.cpp",
						"startLine": "200",
						"endLine": "200",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"m_surface.getTexture"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"texture_id\": \"texture_obj_0x123abc\", \"size\": {\"width\": 800, \"height\": 600}, \"content\": \"rendered_scene_pixels\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"texture_id\": \"texture_obj_0x123abc\", \"size\": {\"width\": 800, \"height\": 600}, \"content\": \"rendered_scene_pixels\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "495cbc79-5a19-4587-842a-8acdf3c63242",
					"diagramNodeId": "3aa6d527-8cf4-4117-9f93-83db7a6e8f2a",
					"simStepLabel": "Retrieve Texture for Post-Processing",
					"simStepDescription": "The `getTexture()` method is called on the `sf::RenderTexture` to obtain a constant reference to its internal, up-to-date texture. This texture is then used to construct a `sf::Sprite` for rendering to the main window.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "include/SFML/Graphics/RenderTexture.hpp",
						"startLine": "253",
						"endLine": "264",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"getTexture",
							"m_texture"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"renderTextureObject\": \"m_surface\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"texture_ref\": \"texture_obj_0x123abc\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "7218b401-8dff-45af-9e79-20db9673f026",
					"diagramNodeId": "b5cccff8-6881-49c2-990a-987abca4068d",
					"simStepLabel": "Prepare Sprite and Shader for Final Draw",
					"simStepDescription": "A `sf::Sprite` is created using the texture from the `RenderTexture`. `RenderStates` are configured to use a post-processing shader. This package of data (sprite using the off-screen texture, and shader states) is prepared to be sent to the main window's `draw` method.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "examples/shader/Shader.cpp",
						"startLine": "199",
						"endLine": "200",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"states.shader",
							"m_shader",
							"sf::Sprite",
							"m_surface.getTexture"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"sprite\": {\"texture_id\": \"texture_obj_0x123abc\"}, \"render_states\": {\"shader\": \"edge_shader.frag\", \"blendMode\": \"BlendAlpha\"}}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"sprite\": {\"texture_id\": \"texture_obj_0x123abc\"}, \"render_states\": {\"shader\": \"edge_shader.frag\", \"blendMode\": \"BlendAlpha\"}}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "8b1e1da3-64fd-49fc-842b-e7c955b29489",
					"diagramNodeId": "251f4d40-b6aa-4542-b5e3-ce7444271f27",
					"simStepLabel": "Draw to Main Window with Post-Processing Shader",
					"simStepDescription": "The main `sf::RenderWindow`'s `draw` method is called. It is passed the sprite containing the off-screen texture and render states that specify the post-processing shader. The SFML rendering pipeline draws this sprite to the window's back buffer, applying the fragment shader to every pixel of the texture.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "examples/shader/Shader.cpp",
						"startLine": "198",
						"endLine": "201",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"target.draw",
							"sf::Sprite",
							"m_surface.getTexture()",
							"states",
							"m_shader"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"sprite\": {\"texture_id\": \"texture_obj_0x123abc\"}, \"render_states\": {\"shader\": \"edge_shader.frag\"}}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"window_framebuffer\": \"contains_post_processed_scene\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "597b4b48-d72f-4621-be01-9ee65378c6cb",
					"diagramNodeId": "ddff60df-5173-436c-bf11-054506186945",
					"simStepLabel": "Final Frame Ready for Display",
					"simStepDescription": "The window's back buffer now holds the complete, rendered frame, ready to be displayed on the screen. The `display()` call will present this buffer.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "examples/shader/Shader.cpp",
						"startLine": "497",
						"endLine": "497",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"window.draw",
							"currentEffect"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"window_framebuffer\": \"contains_post_processed_scene\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"window_framebuffer\": \"contains_post_processed_scene\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "4c311c59-24ba-478c-af81-5c73902ba570",
					"diagramNodeId": "03f05d13-da4b-4f30-baf3-e9a8dac2ef90",
					"simStepLabel": "Display Final Image on Screen",
					"simStepDescription": "The `display()` method of the `sf::RenderWindow` is called. This swaps the back buffer (which contains the post-processed image) with the front buffer, making the final frame visible to the user.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "examples/shader/Shader.cpp",
						"startLine": "517",
						"endLine": "517",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"window.display"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"window_framebuffer\": \"contains_post_processed_scene\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"screen_output\": \"final_image_is_visible_to_user\"}"
				}
			],
			"description": "<ul><li>This feature enables rendering the entire scene or parts of it to an intermediate texture instead of directly to the window, allowing for advanced graphical techniques</li><li>- Create an <code>sf::RenderTexture</code> as a drawing target</li><li>- Draw multiple objects (sprites, shapes, etc</li><li>) to this off-screen texture</li><li>- Apply post-processing effects, such as a full-screen blur or color grading shader, to the texture</li><li>- Draw the final, modified texture to the main window</li></ul>",
			"simulationNodesAndEdges": {
				"1fa55cb6-f31f-4675-9a6e-fc7b21c6e310": {
					"simStepIds": [
