		"Manage 2D views for camera control and UI overlays": {
			"name": "Manage 2D views for camera control and UI overlays",
			"simSteps": [
				{
					"simStepId": "fec1e926-9641-4251-974f-62f2eab1a155",
					"diagramNodeId": "6ad4b3df-4215-47b7-9339-1d6c1f68a1e5",
					"simStepLabel": "Flow 1: Event Handling - Window Resize Event",
					"simStepDescription": "The application's main loop polls for events. When a window resize event occurs, the application logic creates a new `sf::View` to adjust the game's viewport to the new window dimensions, ensuring the content scales correctly.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "examples/tennis/Tennis.cpp",
						"startLine": "152",
						"endLine": "158",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"event",
							"view",
							"window"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"event\": {\"type\": \"Resized\", \"size\": {\"width\": 1280, \"height\": 720}}}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"viewConfig\": {\"size\": {\"width\": 1024, \"height\": 768}, \"center\": {\"x\": 512, \"y\": 384}}}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "e18f1a26-a2fe-4bb2-8edd-72df93127c82",
					"diagramNodeId": "deca5615-7641-4b95-939c-ccb1fd8ddc5f",
					"simStepLabel": "Flow 1: Data Transmission - View Object to Render Window",
					"simStepDescription": "The newly configured `sf::View` object, which now matches the new window size, is passed to the `sf::RenderWindow::setView` method to be applied.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "examples/tennis/Tennis.cpp",
						"startLine": "157",
						"endLine": "157",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"window",
							"view"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"view\": {\"center\": {\"x\": 512, \"y\": 384}, \"size\": {\"width\": 1024, \"height\": 768}, \"rotation\": 0, \"viewport\": {\"left\": 0, \"top\": 0, \"width\": 1, \"height\": 1}}}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"view\": {\"center\": {\"x\": 512, \"y\": 384}, \"size\": {\"width\": 1024, \"height\": 768}, \"rotation\": 0, \"viewport\": {\"left\": 0, \"top\": 0, \"width\": 1, \"height\": 1}}}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "9f41a771-a341-4f62-89ac-4ff1b91e5066",
					"diagramNodeId": "254d835e-a216-49ae-b94e-ef27399bf403",
					"simStepLabel": "Flow 1: API Call - Update RenderTarget's View",
					"simStepDescription": "The `sf::RenderTarget::setView` method is invoked. It updates the render target's internal `sf::View` instance with the new view and sets a flag (`m_cache.viewChanged`) to true, indicating that the rendering projection needs to be recalculated before the next draw call.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/SFML/Graphics/RenderTarget.cpp",
						"startLine": "255",
						"endLine": "259",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"view",
							"m_view",
							"m_cache.viewChanged"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"view\": {\"center\": {\"x\": 512, \"y\": 384}, \"size\": {\"width\": 1024, \"height\": 768}}}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"m_view\": {\"center\": {\"x\": 512, \"y\": 384}, \"size\": {\"width\": 1024, \"height\": 768}}, \"m_cache.viewChanged\": true}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "fe594bf8-b634-444a-952c-1b1ca3e11e36",
					"diagramNodeId": "2f886da1-91dd-40d2-8664-1524baf76b4a",
					"simStepLabel": "Flow 2: Data Transmission - Character Position for Camera Pan",
					"simStepDescription": "The updated position of a game entity (e.g., the player's character) is determined. This position vector will be used to update the camera's center, making the view follow the entity.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "include/SFML/Graphics/View.hpp",
						"startLine": "80",
						"endLine": "80",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"center"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"characterPosition\": {\"x\": 450.5, \"y\": 320.0}}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"characterPosition\": {\"x\": 450.5, \"y\": 320.0}}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "b9fffd01-207b-4116-a63d-33b1315600f6",
					"diagramNodeId": "cb81c998-e644-44b0-be45-12e389a56845",
					"simStepLabel": "Flow 2: API Call - Set View Center (Panning)",
					"simStepDescription": "The application calls `sf::View::setCenter` with the character's new position. This method updates the view's internal center coordinates and invalidates the cached transformation matrices by setting `m_transformUpdated` and `m_invTransformUpdated` to `false`.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/SFML/Graphics/View.cpp",
						"startLine": "48",
						"endLine": "53",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"center",
							"m_center",
							"m_transformUpdated",
							"m_invTransformUpdated"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"center\": {\"x\": 450.5, \"y\": 320.0}}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"m_center\": {\"x\": 450.5, \"y\": 320.0}, \"m_transformUpdated\": false, \"m_invTransformUpdated\": false}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "37fdc92f-f0ce-45d4-964f-777cd85b0cb8",
					"diagramNodeId": "a76e992b-4144-4602-8f22-7bba12ea20e1",
					"simStepLabel": "Flow 2: Data Transmission - Apply Panned View",
					"simStepDescription": "The modified `sf::View` object, now centered on the character, is passed back to the `sf::RenderWindow` via `setView` to apply the changes for the upcoming frame.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "include/SFML/Graphics/RenderTarget.hpp",
						"startLine": "147",
						"endLine": "147",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"setView",
							"view"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"view\": {\"center\": {\"x\": 450.5, \"y\": 320.0}, \"size\": {\"width\": 1024, \"height\": 768}}}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"view\": {\"center\": {\"x\": 450.5, \"y\": 320.0}, \"size\": {\"width\": 1024, \"height\": 768}}}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "053fa3fa-5441-47e3-a3a8-691cd385d118",
					"diagramNodeId": "eecc515e-1d43-4c53-9281-d1405689d826",
					"simStepLabel": "Flow 2: API Call - Update RenderTarget with Panned View",
					"simStepDescription": "The `sf::RenderTarget::setView` method is called again, copying the panned view into its internal state and flagging that the view has changed, ensuring the new camera position is used for rendering.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/SFML/Graphics/RenderTarget.cpp",
						"startLine": "255",
						"endLine": "259",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"view",
							"m_view",
							"m_cache.viewChanged"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"view\": {\"center\": {\"x\": 450.5, \"y\": 320.0}}}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"m_cache.viewChanged\": true}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "c9c32628-7095-4215-8774-3485fc44b99b",
					"diagramNodeId": "1fdff70d-eb8d-4a13-86d0-564cfd480e3a",
					"simStepLabel": "Flow 3: Data Transmission - Zoom Factor",
					"simStepDescription": "Based on user input like a mouse scroll wheel, a zoom factor is determined. A factor greater than 1 zooms out (objects appear smaller), and a factor less than 1 zooms in (objects appear larger).",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "include/SFML/Graphics/View.hpp",
						"startLine": "232",
						"endLine": "232",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"factor"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"factor\": 0.8}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"factor\": 0.8}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "9d1fc73f-ac3e-4acc-b1a7-175b5f7bd20a",
					"diagramNodeId": "612c7a69-65d6-48d8-8238-0127aa9d9fdd",
					"simStepLabel": "Flow 3: API Call - Zoom View",
					"simStepDescription": "The application calls the `sf::View::zoom` method with the specified factor. This is a convenience function that multiplies the current view's size by the factor and calls `setSize` internally.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/SFML/Graphics/View.cpp",
						"startLine": "147",
						"endLine": "150",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"factor",
							"setSize",
							"m_size"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"factor\": 0.8, \"current_size\": {\"width\": 1000, \"height\": 1000}}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"new_size\": {\"width\": 800, \"height\": 800}}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "963602e7-5c85-461e-80d4-4759cd13d36b",
					"diagramNodeId": "05b2f33b-53db-4af3-91b1-6a7f19aa6783",
					"simStepLabel": "Flow 3: Data Transmission - Apply Zoomed View",
					"simStepDescription": "The `sf::View` object, which has been resized to simulate a zoom, is passed back to the `sf::RenderWindow` to be applied for the next rendering frame.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "include/SFML/Graphics/RenderTarget.hpp",
						"startLine": "147",
						"endLine": "147",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"setView",
							"view"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"view\": {\"center\": {\"x\": 450.5, \"y\": 320.0}, \"size\": {\"width\": 800, \"height\": 800}}}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"view\": {\"center\": {\"x\": 450.5, \"y\": 320.0}, \"size\": {\"width\": 800, \"height\": 800}}}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "a0766046-3fc4-450d-9391-de86a22a23be",
					"diagramNodeId": "94a3e70d-5466-4ef0-9fed-fe254dfc17a9",
					"simStepLabel": "Flow 3: API Call - Update RenderTarget with Zoomed View",
					"simStepDescription": "Finally, `sf::RenderTarget::setView` is called with the zoomed view. The render target updates its internal view and flags it as changed, so the new zoom level will be reflected in subsequent draw calls.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/SFML/Graphics/RenderTarget.cpp",
						"startLine": "255",
						"endLine": "259",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"view",
							"m_view",
							"m_cache.viewChanged"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"view\": {\"size\": {\"width\": 800, \"height\": 800}}}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"m_cache.viewChanged\": true}"
				}
			],
			"description": "<ul><li>SFML's <code>sf::View</code> class acts as a 2D camera, defining which part of the 2D world is shown on screen</li><li>- Pan the camera by changing the view's center (<code>setCenter</code>) to follow a character or explore a large level</li><li>- Zoom in and out of the scene using <code>zoom()</code></li><li>- Rotate the view for special effects</li><li>- Use multiple views to implement features like split-screen multiplayer or to render a static UI/HUD over a scrolling game world</li></ul>",
			"simulationNodesAndEdges": {
